    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17939" root="زكو" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَكَوِىٌّ</span></b>  [generally meaning <i>Of,</i> or <i>relating to,
the poor-rate</i>] is the rel. n. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَكَاةٌ</span>; like as
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَصَوِىٌّ</span> is that of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَصَاةٌ</span>; because the rel. n. reduces the word to its original form: <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَكَائِىٌّ</span> is
vulgar and wrong. (Msb.)

